{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Operator ruling update (2026-08-21, verbatim, attributed to the operator): \"We should suppress the message under normal load. This is noise, not an outage signal.\"\n\nInterpretation recorded with the ruling: under normal load — ordinary contention losses, transient transport retries, and the routine unpushed-backlog suffix — these messages must be SUPPRESSED from agent-visible output entirely (DEBUG at most), not merely reworded at WARNING/INFO. A merely non-zero or shared backlog count is NOT an outage signal. WARNING remains reserved for genuine operator-actionable outage signals only: policy declines, strict-mode failures, and persistent failure clearly beyond normal concurrent-writer contention. The durable marker / fsck PUSH_PENDING observability stays as-is. Reopening to strengthen the ACs and demote the expected-case emissions from INFO to DEBUG."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787341712834542001,"uuid":"ce562ada-2379-41cf-84ba-3a881b0d4cb8"}